+# CONTRACT.md — Real-Time Markdown Collab Server
+
+Definition of done: every checkbox below passes via `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`.
+
+## Build/Lint
+- [ ] `npm run build` — TypeScript compiles with no errors (strict mode)
+- [ ] `npm run lint` — ESLint passes with no errors
+
+## REST CRUD (tests/collab.test.ts "REST CRUD")
+- [ ] POST /docs creates document with title → 201, body.title matches
+- [ ] POST /docs response has id, title, content, created_at, updated_at
+- [ ] GET /docs lists all documents → 200, array
+- [ ] GET /docs/:id returns specific document → 200, matches title
+- [ ] GET /docs/:id 404 for non-existent id
+- [ ] PUT /docs/:id updates title → 200, new title reflected
+- [ ] DELETE /docs/:id removes document → 204, subsequent GET 404
+- [ ] DELETE /docs/:id 404 for non-existent id
+- [ ] GET /docs/:id/versions lists version history, includes version 0 (initial)
+- [ ] GET /docs/:id/versions/:version returns content + version number for that version
+
+## WebSocket Lifecycle
+- [ ] Client connects to ws://.../:docId
+- [ ] On connect, server sends `{type:'sync', content, version}` as first message
+- [ ] Client sends operation → receives `{type:'ack', version}`
+- [ ] Server broadcasts operation to OTHER clients in same doc room as `{type:'operation', operation, ...}`
+- [ ] Sending client does NOT receive its own op back (gets ack only)
+- [ ] Client disconnect closes cleanly
+- [ ] Multiple (3+) clients can join same document room
+- [ ] Clients in different doc rooms are isolated — no cross-doc leakage
+
+## Single Client Editing (OT apply correctness)
+- [ ] Insert at beginning
+- [ ] Insert at end
+- [ ] Insert in middle
+- [ ] Delete range
+- [ ] Multiple sequential edits accumulate correctly
+- [ ] Version increments strictly after each edit
+
+## Two-Client Convergence (OT transform correctness)
+- [ ] Two clients editing different positions (based on stale version) converge correctly
+- [ ] Two clients inserting at same position: both insertions preserved (length +2, contains both chars)
+- [ ] Insert vs delete concurrent ops both applied, correct result
+- [ ] Rapid alternating edits (5x2=10 ops) converge, final length 10 (no data loss/corruption)
+- [ ] All connected clients see identical content after sync (fetched via REST)
+- [ ] Version history contains all ops in strictly increasing version order
+- [ ] Concurrent edits from stale version do not lose data (both texts present)
+- [ ] Edit at end of doc concurrent with edit at beginning — correct transform via position shift
+
+## Stress (10 concurrent clients)
+- [ ] 10 clients connect to same doc simultaneously without error
+- [ ] 10 clients each send an edit — all 10 edits present in final content, no corruption
+- [ ] After 10 clients sync, reconnecting all 10 shows identical content across all
+- [ ] 50 rapid-fire edits from one client — final length 50, no crash
+- [ ] All 10 clients can disconnect simultaneously without error; server stays healthy
+
+## Error Handling
+- [ ] Connecting to non-existent doc id → first message is `{type:'error', message: contains 'not found'}`
+- [ ] Malformed JSON sent over WS → `{type:'error'}` response, connection survives
+- [ ] Invalid operation type (e.g. 'replace') → `{type:'error'}` response
+- [ ] Out-of-bounds operation (e.g. delete count > remaining length) → `{type:'error'}` response
+- [ ] After malformed input, server remains stable: REST still works, WS still accepts valid ops afterward
+
+## Persistence (SQLite via better-sqlite3, using schema.sql)
+- [ ] Document + content survives server restart (same dbPath)
+- [ ] Version/edit history survives restart (same count)
+- [ ] active_connections table cleared/reset on server start (stale rows from previous run removed)
+
+## Architecture requirements (from TASK.md)
+- [ ] src/db.ts — DB setup applying schema.sql, connection factory
+- [ ] src/models.ts — TS interfaces: Document, Version, Operation (insert/delete)
